# North Star's effect reaches "that spell's mana cost" alone: "Additional costs are still paid normally", and so is a cost
# increase (CR 601.2f, 118.8: the total is the mana cost plus additional costs and increases). Under Bot1's own Derelor
# ("Black spells you cast cost {B} more to cast") Muck Rats costs {B}{B}: two Mountains can't pay it, since red may pay
# the mana cost's {B} but not Derelor's (the refusal is for want of mana: with mana to spare it is offered). Once a Mox
# Jet is there, the two Mountains' red, made first, still leave the increase owed, so the payment asks for the Jet's
# black (CR 601.2g); a Mountain's red pays the mana cost and the black the increase, and one red is left over.

[Bot1 Deck]
North Star
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Muck Rats
Mox Jet
Derelor
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

